{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549897-what-made-u-like-a-particular-clan-over-the-rest","id":1549897,"title":"What made u like a particular clan over the rest?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-06T23:33:56-07:00","id":1549897,"title":"What made u like a particular clan over the rest?","content":"Another fun question for the people here. I like the Malkavians the best as I find oracles and seers interesting and how their insights can unsettle people in general. So what was it that made you like a specific clan over the rest?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T02:42:21-07:00","id":1549902,"title":"","content":"I don't really like any Clan over the rest as they're all great.<br /> <br /> The only exceptions to this is that I don't like Baali, because I don't think they fit my understanding of the Vampire setting as being a dark grey one and I think that the Giovanni makes for a better Necromancer Clan than the Cappadocians.<br /> <br /> The reason as to why I think the Giovanni are better than the Cappadocians is that I find that mafia necromancers gives me more ideas on them as opposed to recclusive scholars.<br /> <br /> One can argue that Giovanni concept steps on the toes of the Ventrue concept but the same is true between the Cappadocians and the Tremere.<br /> <br /> But I'm not saying there's something wrong with the Cappadocians as I like them too, but I find the Giovanni to give me more ideas and the mafia necromancer concept is more interesting than the reclusive scholar/necromancer/mage concept.<br /> <br /> I should disclose that I find organized crime to be a pretty interesting topic and while I'm haven't seen or read extensively on the topic there are lots of ideas there. Sopranos + necromancy makes for a cooler concept with more popular cultural influences and ideas than the Cappadocians, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T04:06:55-07:00","id":1549905,"title":"","content":"I'm quite interested in religion, myth and mystical cults, so Setites grabbed my attention well, especially in their Revised, VDA20, and VtM20 incarnations. I have not delved into V5 enough to have an opinion on the Ministry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T04:20:19-07:00","id":1549906,"title":"","content":"I like the Toreador best because they\u2019re artists and writers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T09:18:50-07:00","id":1549911,"title":"","content":"I have many Clans I really like for various reasons, but the absolute favorite is the Tzimisce<br /> They are part of the local culture and community<br /> I am fortunate becasue my great great grandmother was a &quot;Koldun&quot; - or at least the local equivalent of it, a Solomonari; (could control some Elemental Spirits, they could curse and heal, they could conjure or banish clouds, they could call down hail storms even lightning using their Enchanted axes, spoke with the dead and the spirtis and kept evil at bay. They learned their magic from a mentor and some legends say they even had a school located beyond the shroud) - on our parts they were called &quot;Zeim (variant of Zmei) nitish &quot;Dragon Rider&quot; - and I love the fact it is VERY similar sound of the word Tzimisce<br /> <br /> And Vicissitude not just &quot;merely&quot; an adaption of the Wamphyri from Brian Lumley\u2019s \u201cNecroscope\u201d series in my eyes, again perks of living in that area.<br /> <br /> In South Slavic folklore, a vampire was believed to pass through several distinct stages in its development. The first 40 days were considered decisive for the making of a vampire; it started out as an invisible shadow and then gradually gained strength from the lifeblood of the living, forming a (typically invisible) jelly-like, boneless mass, and eventually building up a human-like body nearly identical to the one the person had had in life. This development allowed the creature to ultimately leave its grave and begin a new life as a human. The vampire, who was usually male, was also sexually active and could have children, either with his widow or a new wife. These could become vampires themselves, but could also have a special ability to see and kill vampires, allowing them to become vampire hunters.<br /> The bodies of vrykolakas have the same distinctive characteristics as the bodies of vampires in Balkan folklore. They do not decay; instead, they swell and may even attain a &quot;drumlike&quot; form, being very large, have a ruddy complexion, and are, according to one account, &quot;fresh and gorged with new blood&quot;.\u200b in Greek folklore, the vrykolakas are described more as cannibals than bloodsuckers with a taste in particular for human livers\u200b<br /> <br /> This a bit obsucre slavic folklore was - I think - where the Tzimisce and their power came from<br /> And of course, the &quot;changing body&quot; is somewhat the base of every vampiric myth; - the natural characteristics of decomposition\u2014such as receding gums and the appearance of growing hair and fingernails\u2014reinforced the belief that corpses were in fact continuing some manner of life after death and transform<br /> <br /> As for the power itself, it actually fits in the following folklore and many other<br /> <br /> Whereas Protean merely enables a Cainite to emulate God's creatures, this twisted power allows a Tzimisce to defile and deform those creatures<br /> \u200bGod's curse is reflected in Vicissitude in that it replaces the ability to nurture and care with the ability to rend and corrupt.<br /> Vicissitude takes the power of creation, how God created Adam and Lilith from the living earth, formed them like a sculptor using clay, Vicissitude twist this holy creation with the twisting and shaping God's perfect creation - after all, Genesis told us, God created man in his own image<br /> <br /> My other favorite is the Kiasyd<br /> I just love those &quot;Elven&quot; Vampires, their ties to the Dreaming (or nightmare...). They are a bridge between several games and I love crossovers!<br /> <br /> The third is the Followers of Set, like Hermeticus, I found them camptivating esepcially in Revised, VDA20, and VtM20<br /> And still firmly belive they are essentially rigt and not Cainites at all, but the Egyptian equivalent of Kuei-Jin<br /> Actually the Followers of Set should be like the Kuei-jin, but instead of the Thousand Hell of Yomi a potential Settie should be an escapee from Duat - the egyptian underworld basically Hell if you are not in a tiny portion of it aka. manage to gain acces to the Field of Reeds, where Osiris rules<br /> Serpents, the spawn of Apep, haunt the 12 caverns of Duat. They swim in the river and coil about the limbs of the unredeemed dead.<br /> The dead in Duat exist in darkness, blinded by it, relieved only by the nightly passage of the ship of Ra<br /> Along with their torments, the dead in Duat cannot breathe or speak. The &quot;Opening of the Mouth&quot; funerary ritual was meant to deliver the deceased from this unhappy condition.<br /> The dead in Duat rest in coffins, paralized, that open only when the sun-god Ra makes his nightly passage.<br /> Just to name a few<br /> Duat is... not the nicest place, it is literally Hell if you don't cheat your way thrugh it, filled with darkness, silence, sand, snakes, demons and quite nasty things even the Sun God have to fight and Mandjet, the <i>Boat</i> of <i>Millions of Years</i>\u200b needs quite a fighter crew to help him out (and the mightiest of them was <b>Sutekh...</b>)... even the domain of <b>Seker</b>, the original God of the Underworld whom Osiris basically dethroned, Imhet was seen as difficult, sandy terrain, not to mention according to the myth, Seker rules the Fifth Kingdom of Night, which is called &quot;Hidden&quot;, and is tasked with punishing the souls of evildoers by throwing them into a boiling lake. Only a tiny part is &quot;good&quot;, the Field of Reeds and the personal domain of Osiris... and there is the whole Scales and Feather of Ma'at against your heart, the 42 Judges who destroy you if you don't know their name, <b>Ammit</b> eagerly awaits to eat your soul if you fail the Scales<br /> And thats for the &quot;normal dead&quot;!<br /> However, when the damned died? Their flesh was torn away by demons and their mummy wrappings were removed so that their bodies were left to decompose. In the underworld that the blessed successfully navigate, their order of things is reversed, even to the extent that the damned have to walk upside down, eat their own excrement and drink their own urine. Their hands are tied behind their backs, often around stakes. Their heads and limbs are severed from their bodies and their flesh is cut off their bones. Their hearts are removed and their ba-souls are separated from their bodies, forever unable to return to them. They even loose their shadows, which were considered an important part of the ancient Egyptian being. They have no air and suffer from hunger and thirst, as they receive no funerary offerings. Worst of all, they are denied the reviving light of the sun god, who ignores them, even as they cry out load and wail when he passes them in the underworld at night.<br /> They are continuously punished by demons, who are the representatives of chaos. Indeed, the demons are often recruited from the ranks of the damned themselves, so that they torture and kill one another. They are subjected to knives and swords and to the fire of hell, often kindled by fire spitting snakes. These horrible punishments were carried out in the &quot;slaughtering place&quot; or &quot;place of destruction&quot;, and presided over by the fierce goddess <b>Sekhmet</b>, whose butchers hack their victims to pieces and burn them with inextinguishable fire, sometimes in deep pits or in cauldrons in which they are scorched, cooked and reduced to ashes. Demons feed on their entrails and drink their blood.<br /> Another location was the Lake of Fire, which was first mentioned in the Book of Two Ways in the Coffin Text (Spell 1054/1166) and illustrated in the Book of the Dead (Chapter 126). Like the &quot;outer darkness,&quot; it is a place of regeneration for the sun god and his blessed followers, to whom it provides nourishment and cool water, but a place of destruction for the damned. Birds even fly away from it when they experience the burning, bloody water and small the stench of putrefaction which rises from it. In chapter 126 of the Book of the Dead, its shores are guarded by four baboons who sit at the bow of the barque of Ra and who are usually connected to the sunrise. There, they act as judges of the divine tribunal in order to decide who might be granted access through &quot;the secret portals of the West&quot; and who will be delivered to the hellhound, who, according to another spell, is in charge of this place. That demon-god is the &quot;Swallower of Millions,&quot; responsible for devouring corpses, or their shadows, snatching hearts and inflicting injury without being seen (<b>Am-heh</b> was a dangerous god from the underworld whose name can be translated as 'devourer of millions', or eater of eternity. He lived in a lake of fire and was represented as a man with the head of a hunting dog.)<br /> Not to mention <b>Shezmu</b>\u200b, Demon-God of the Wine Press, Oils and Slaughterer of the Damned; after the deceased had died, it was he who caught the sinful ones for punishment. In Chapter 175 of The Book of the Dead Shesmu was known as &quot;Lord of the Blood&quot;. It was under the orders of Osiris, that he would chop up the evil ones, take their heads and toss them into a wine press, treating the heads as if they were grapes to create blood wine.<br /> \u200b<br /> The judgement of Ma'at and devoured by Ammit was actually an &quot;easy death&quot; compared others\u200b<br /> <br /> In this regard Sutekh came back from Hell, like the souls come back/escape from Yomi. Apophis (and even other gods of Duat) like the Yama Kings<br /> The Followers of Set calls themselves the Mesu Bedshet, the &quot;<i>Children</i> of <i>Rebellion</i>&quot; for a reason - with a twist, this makes the Children of Anubis, the Silent Striders technically the jailors of Duat/Hell the &quot;bad guys&quot; and enemies of the Followers of Set, just they forgot the reason\u200b<br /> <br /> Would make much more sense, considering the whole belief system of the Followers of Sutekh to be like the Kuei-jin rather like the get of Caine<br /> Or actually sell Sutekh as Caine... the murdering of thy brother is a tiny bit older story with Sutekh and Asar/Set and Osiris than Caine and Abel...<br /> <br /> God I just love them\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T15:39:00-07:00","id":1549926,"title":"","content":"I was a fan of the notion that Set is the originator of the vampire race. I also like the idea that Caine cursed Malkav with madness to shut him up as he learned that the Dark Father was not the first of his kind, but the last survivor of an earlier group of Kindred and that Gehenna happens in cycles with whomever is left becoming the new source of &quot;race&quot;and they can make up whatever they want to the newer generations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T09:41:45-07:00","id":1549966,"title":"","content":"I think that I have always been the most drawn to the Tremere. In large part, I liked their competence and taking vampirism seriously. They are highly organized, scholarly, ruthless, dedicated. I like how they are like a secret society, I like the pyramid structure, the rituals, the secret societies with secret societies, the dichotomy of Clan loyalty versus self interested advancement. I just really like them a lot.<br /> <br /> Even though they are rivals within the setting, I like the Tzimisce a lot as well. Especially Old Clan Tzimisce. I like the connection to the land, the hyper-traditionalism, the honor combined with harsh cruelty, the mystical elements. I like Dracula. I like the Revenant families.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T11:00:20-07:00","id":1549969,"title":"","content":"I like the Old Clan Tziscme myself a great deal, but I have never used them myself yet. One day soon I hope something will click for an NPC at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T05:06:03-07:00","id":1549999,"title":"","content":"As a trans person who struggled with dysphoria for decades, I have particular fondness for the Nosferatu. And as a romantic who's in love with being in love, I find that the Toreador speak to me as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T20:34:57-07:00","id":1550023,"title":"","content":"My three favorite clans have always been the Followers of Set, the Cappadocians and the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> The Followers of Set have a lot of really interesting lore around them. The idea that Set was originally a 4th generation vampire who diablarizred one of the third generation to create his own clan is kind of cool. Then you have the idea that there are somewhat periodic purges, and hinted ideas at a war between Typhon and Set, etc. Plus the whole Conan/Egyptian vibe is pretty cool. The only thing I wish they had played a bit more with was the idea of religious conflict within the clan. There should be inquisitions and schisms and such. Instead the clan was generally always presented as to being on the same page, which always bugged me a bit. The split/rebranding into the Ministry in 5th edition is definitely my favorite thing to come out of the new edition and it's something that I include in every other VtM game I run. <br /> <br /> For the Cappadocians I've always thought Necromancy was pretty cool, and it opens up a lot of cool actions and idea via the Wraith game. The Cappadocians, as a nearly extinct clan in the modern nights, always felt a bit cooler to me than the Giovanni. Plus, in lore, there were a lot of issues with the Giovanni (they could only have 3 vampires sired each generation, they didn't really have anything to do with any of the other factions, etc) which tended to make them a bit harder to play or use.<br /> <br /> Finally for the Tzimisce, they're just the classic concept of a noble vampire, with the addition to Vissicitude, which is just about the coolest power in the game. Lore wise they also have the Path of Metamorphosis, which inhabits some really cool conceptual space where a vampire seeks to embrace and transcend their inhumanity to become something alien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T22:14:09-07:00","id":1550024,"title":"","content":"My next favorite clan is Followers of Set as I love Egyptian historical fiction from writer Wilbur Smith and I wanted to see how there version of Set was going to be depicted and I like them as the wildcard element of Kindred society who might know unpleasant truths of Kindred origins and that Caine might have been lying about being the first of the vampire race.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T17:08:12-07:00","id":1550128,"title":"","content":"I liked the Gangrel and the Ventrue, but, I didn't care for Toreadors or Malks. I considered Brujah vamps as Lost Boys. Nos, were just weird; but, I like Thaumaturgy, especially out of the Player's Guide. I like Gangrel's protean, and Ventures seemed like true vampires. I first read about vamps, in Ann Rice books, so I don't have a Clan-mentality. I especially like the clans out of Requiem; I like the mystery of their origins, and their weakness are better (penalties for, say social-rolls, for Nos)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}